    "statement": "The singleton fraction falls monotonically from 83.9 % at 250 m to 35.3 % at 2000 m, so it DOES drop below 40 % — but only once clustering has stopped being clustering: at 2000 m the largest cluster holds 91 of 174 points (52 %), and at 3000 m it holds 168 of 174 (97 %). Restricting to radii where no cluster exceeds 25% of all rescue points, the singleton fraction never goes below 49.2 %. Dispersion is a measured property of the sampled origin set here, not an untuned parameter."
